=== Train shed ===

The train shed covers the 30 at-grade tracks and 20 platforms and is a large iron-and-glass structure spanning the full width of the platform area. The shed's ironwork is executed in the Volisanian colonial tradition, with riveted iron trusses and ornamental detailing at the column capitals, while the glazed panels incorporate decorative leadwork patterns that echo Zong geometric motifs. The shed provides natural light to the platforms below through its glazed roof, which is arranged in a series of longitudinal ridges running the length of the platforms.

